  "answer": "This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys has no context menu editor, and the main tracker for it is PowerToys#33. When a similar ticket (PowerToys#46748) was filed, it was closed as a duplicate of #33. Please add your +1 and your details, such as hiding rarely used entries and promoting items like 'create desktop shortcut', to #33. The ticket doesn't promise a delivery date. Until then, you can use third-party tools. The #33 discussion mentions ContextMenuManager, which works on the old menu only. It also mentions NileSoft Shell, which can remove entries. Some of the entries you listed, such as the phone link and the Notepad and Notepad++ items, are added by Windows or by other apps, not by PowerToys."
 },
